What is a Hydraulic Robot?
Hydraulic robots are industrial robotic platforms that use high‑pressure hydraulic fluid to actuate their joints and axes. Compared with electric actuators, hydraulic systems provide a superior power‑to‑weight ratio, enabling payload capacities that often exceed 200 kg and, in specialised designs, more than 500 kg. This makes them indispensable for applications where raw force, robustness and continuous torque are paramount, such as forging presses, large‑scale material handling, offshore installation and heavy‑duty assembly lines.

